{%- comment -%}
  The fetch endpoint behind the All Collections section's tabs, and nothing
  else. It has no presets, so it never appears in the editor's section list.

  A tab is a link to a real collection, and the script asks that link's URL
  for this section:

      /collections/cleansers?section_id=all-collections-grid

  Shopify renders it in that URL's context, which is the whole trick — the
  section does not have to be told which collection to draw, because
  `collection` already is one. It also does not have to exist on that
  collection's template: `?section_id=` resolves against the section file.

  The wrapper below is what the script reads. The `<div>` Shopify puts around
  every rendered section would do, but naming the element the script wants
  means a change to that wrapper cannot quietly break the swap.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div data-acl-items>
  {%- if collection != blank -%}
    {% render 'all-collections-grid', grid_collection: collection, section_id: section.id %}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "All Collections grid"
}
{% endschema %}
